     "line": 141,
     "quote": "CFE_MSG_CommandHeader_t Cmd;",
     "why": "The union exposes the command header and base message as directly accessible members, so user code can depend on the current header layout and type-punning. If cFE changes CFE_MSG_CommandHeader_t fields, order, alignment, or the base message representation, users that read or cast Cmd/BaseMsg must change."
    },
